#
# The per-cycle stream roll-up. A single overwritten marker file cannot
# accumulate, which is why a partial PROVE tranche used to be refused outright
# and why the coverage-drop warning compared "the previous write of this file"
# rather than cycle N-1. Partial records are now accepted and stored, both
# tranches of a two-part PROVE survive (AC-020 / OT-009), the >=95% thresholds
# are evaluated once per cycle at the streams-complete check against the cycle
# total, and drop warnings compare cycle N to cycle N-1 -- so a second tranche
# of the SAME cycle is no longer a false alarm.
#
# Also FR-020 / AC-025's auto-VERIFY hole, which lives in the same
# _prove_is_clean read path: a spec parsing to ZERO requirements used to skip
# the coverage check entirely, so any clean .prove-complete drove the F4
# auto-pass on a spec nothing had been proved against.
